        "id": 18278,
        "name": "Godai",
        "username": "Godai",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/godai/{size}/1920_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-07-25T21:24:05.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Just finished watching the latest Sentinel Comics Live stream, and I had an idea for something useful that might be added to the Kickstarter. In the spirit of Co-Op, let’s fill this post with cool things we would like to see come Kickstarter time!</p><p>I’ll start with my mid-game observation:</p><p><strong>THE DECK OF MODS AND MINIONS</strong></p><p>Basically, a custom card deck add-on that contains:</p><ul>\n<li>a bunch of double sided Modifier Cards (+1 on one side, -1 on the other, up to +4/-4), maybe a few with “Persistent” on them,</li>\n<li>a bunch of cards that say “Minions” with a d4 or d6 or d-whatever printed below, and “Lieutenant” on the reverse side with the same die size,</li>\n<li>a handful of double sided cards that read “Green Zone” &amp; “Yellow Zone” and “Red Zone” &amp; “Out”, enough for all players</li>\n</ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The concept being that those index cards are super useful, but why keep writing them out over and over? And in a perfect world, the cards would be printed on a material you could use wet erase and/or dry erase markers on, for on the fly notations.</p><p>How feasible is this? No clue, but at least the idea is out there for GTG to consider, if they haven’t already. Any other ideas to throw at them over the next six months?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:51:34.321Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
