        "raw": "<p>Just finished watching the latest Sentinel Comics Live stream, and I had an idea for something useful that might be added to the Kickstarter. In the spirit of Co-Op, let&rsquo;s fill this post with cool things we would like to see come Kickstarter time!</p><p>I&rsquo;ll start with my mid-game observation:</p><p><strong>THE DECK OF MODS AND MINIONS</strong></p><p>Basically, a custom card deck add-on that contains:</p><ul><li>a bunch of double sided Modifier Cards (+1 on one side, -1 on the other, up to +4/-4), maybe a few with &ldquo;Persistent&rdquo; on them,</li><li>a bunch of cards that say &ldquo;Minions&rdquo; with a d4 or d6 or d-whatever printed below, and &ldquo;Lieutenant&rdquo; on the reverse side with the same die size,</li><li>a handful of double sided cards that read &ldquo;Green Zone&rdquo; &amp; &ldquo;Yellow Zone&rdquo; and &ldquo;Red Zone&rdquo; &amp; &ldquo;Out&rdquo;, enough for all players</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The concept being that those index cards are super useful, but why keep writing them out over and over? And in a perfect world, the cards would be printed on a material you could use wet erase and/or dry erase markers on, for on the fly notations.</p><p>How feasible is this? No clue, but at least the idea is out there for GTG to consider, if they haven&rsquo;t already. Any other ideas to throw at them over the next six months?</p>",
