        "id": 220588,
        "name": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-07-26T20:17:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Matchstickman\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/48/1880_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Matchstickman:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Hire PlatinumWarlock to write something.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Wow–I'm flattered!&nbsp; Thanks for the vote of confidence!</p>\n<p>In all reality, though, I got a chance to chat briefly with Christopher (and Craig) at Origins.&nbsp; I've made a standing offer to work on any Dark Watch-type sourcebook (or, perhaps, an Extremiverse book).&nbsp; Note that there is no contract signed, no confirmation of such a book even existed–just an offer on my part that I'd be willing and able to work on such a thing, if they needed freelance writers.</p>\n<p>For that matter, I'd happily offer up my \"Villain of the Day\" as a subsidiary rogues' gallery, if there was interest in including a 'rogues gallery' type sourcebook.</p>",
