        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-07-26T20:38:37.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>In not-me related ideas, how about this:</p><p>A series of interlocking plastic 1-inch tiles that you could lay flat on the table:&nbsp; maybe 8 green, 8 yellow, and 8 red in a pack.&nbsp; Using these, you can create a physical representation of the scene tracker, customizable as you need for the scene.&nbsp; Then, you could use either a pointer tracker (or maybe include a translucent token to sit on top of the tile) to display which segment of the scene the players are in.</p>",
