        "id": 220591,
        "name": "KateWalker",
        "username": "TakeWalker",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-07-26T22:32:19.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"PlatinumWarlock\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/48/1869_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> PlatinumWarlock:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In not-me related ideas, how about this:A series of interlocking plastic 1-inch tiles that you could lay flat on the table:&nbsp; maybe 8 green, 8 yellow, and 8 red in a pack.&nbsp; Using these, you can create a physical representation of the scene tracker, customizable as you need for the scene.&nbsp; Then, you could use either a pointer tracker (or maybe include a translucent token to sit on top of the tile) to display which segment of the scene the players are in.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Hey, if you can snap 'em together, you could snap 'em apart, crumbling bridge style. Have miniatures representing the heroes to further hammer home the comparison! :V</p>",
        "post_number": 8,
        "post_type": 1,
